The code description.

Key Changes and Considerations:

Wind Sensor Pins: Defines WIND_SPEED_PIN and WIND_DIR_PIN for the anemometer and wind vane.
Wind Speed Variables: Added variables for tracking wind speed pulses and timing (wind_pulse_count, last_wind_sample_time, current_wind_sample_time, wind_sample_period). The wind_sample_period is set to 5 seconds, but you can adjust this.
Interrupt for Wind Speed: The windPulseCounter() function is attached to the interrupt for the WIND_SPEED_PIN. This function increments the wind_pulse_count every time a pulse is detected from the anemometer. Make sure the interrupt pin can handle pulses.
calculateWindSpeed(): Calculates wind speed in MPH based on the number of pulses within the sample period, using the formula provided.
calculateWindDirection(): Calculates wind direction in degrees (0-360) based on the analog reading from the WIND_DIR_PIN. Important: This function assumes a linear relationship between resistance and angle, which might not be accurate for all wind vanes. You will need to calibrate this function based on the specific resistance-to-angle characteristics of your wind vane sensor. I've added some example resistance ranges and angles, but these are placeholders.
Sensor Data Collection: The GetSensorData() function now reads the wind speed and direction:
It reads the analog value from the wind direction pin.
It calculates wind speed and direction using the helper functions.
It stores the calculated values in the data JSON document.
The wind speed and direction are only calculated and updated every wind_sample_period seconds.
Data Logging and Submission: The LogDataToSerial() and WriteDataToSD() functions now include the wind speed and direction values.
New Parameter Labels: Added WIND_SPEED and WIND_DIRECTION to the parameters.h file (which you should create).
